   "he": "וְלֹא יַעֲבוֹר תַּחְתֶּיהָ, וְאִם עָבַר — טָמֵא. מַאי טַעְמָא? אִי אֶפְשָׁר דְּלֵיכָּא תִּקְרוֹבֶת עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And one may not pass beneath» an ashera, «and if one passed» beneath it he is «ritually impure.» The Gemara asks: «What is the reason?» The Gemara answers: Because «it is impossible that there is no» remnant of an «idolatrous offering» underneath the tree."
